{"nodes": [{"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "label": "Perflo AP Agent PRD v0", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-26T00:00:00Z", "author": "Hemant Kumar", "contributor": "Yeshu Agarwal", "rationale": null}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_composio", "label": "Composio (Gmail Connector)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_gmail", "label": "Gmail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_postgres", "label": "PostgreSQL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_perflo_cli", "label": "Perflo CLI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_x402", "label": "x402 Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invoice links are opened only in Perflo's x402 headless browser - a clean, paid, isolated session where the vendor eats the risk of rendering attacker-controlled pages. The browser output stays untrusted. Never open a link with the app's own fetch or the owner's browser session."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_ap_agent", "label": "Perflo AP Agent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A queue, not a chatbot: CFO teams want to see the triggers, the steps and the failures, with an agent handling the smart parts in between. 'I want an agent, not an app' - a database, a worker with cron jobs, an LLM agent with tools for judgement, deterministic code for everything that touches money."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_ingest_worker", "label": "Ingest Worker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dedupe on gmail_message_id so a message is ingested once, ever. Composio triggers get missed, so polling has to exist anyway."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_classifier", "label": "Classifier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cheap code pass drops obvious noise first; the LLM then sorts the rest with no tools, so an injected instruction in the body cannot steer it. Untrusted content sits inside delimiters in the prompt."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_extractor", "label": "Extractor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sandboxed (no tools), structured JSON output only with a confidence per field. Free text from a model never becomes a parameter to Perflo."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_payee_resolver", "label": "Payee Resolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exact-match rule: auto-pay only if the sender identity maps to an approved payee AND the extracted payment-details hash equals the stored approved method. 'This one rule kills most business email compromise on its own.' Mappings are never inferred; they exist only because the owner approved them."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_verifier", "label": "Verifier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invoice fraud is the single most common way businesses lose money; any AP automation that pays what it reads is a machine for losing money faster. The verifier is not a feature on top - it is the reason this thing is safe to run unattended. It returns an evidence bundle and never decides to pay."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_policy_engine", "label": "Policy Engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The money decision is deterministic code, never an LLM: auto_pay only when all FR-19 checks hold (classification, extraction confidence, exact payee match, auth, verifier score, no duplicate, grant caps, ceiling, not paused). The LLM never executes money directly."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_payment_executor", "label": "Payment Executor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Idempotency key (sha256 of message, payee method, amount, currency, reference) enforced by a unique index, and a single writer per intent via row locks. Unknown outcome means 'assume it was sent' until the reconciler proves otherwise. The owner's two failure modes - an agent that pays twice inside guardrails - are what this component exists to prevent."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_reconciler", "label": "Reconciler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolves paying/unknown_outcome/paid intents from perflo activity and tx status. Never re-pays anything."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_notifier", "label": "Notifier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Approval emails come from the app's own sender, never the owner's Gmail, and carry one signed single-use link - no approve button in the email itself, and no payment details an attacker would want to learn."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_queue_ui", "label": "Queue UI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Business owners and CFOs want a table/queue - Queued, Needs Approval, Auto-Paid, Quarantined, Duplicate - not a chatbot. A chat box can come last, if at all."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_prompt_injection", "label": "Anti-Prompt Injection Controls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The LLM extractor is sandboxed (no tools) and parses the email inside delimiters; the system flags the injection and moves the email to quarantined. Structured output only; injection snippets must appear in the evidence."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_grant_guardrail", "label": "Perflo Grant Guardrail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The owner approves each payee once in their own browser with caps (per payment, total, count, expiry). Even if every LLM in the system is fooled, money can only go to a recipient the owner approved, up to those caps. Don't design anything that routes around it - there is no 'pay to arbitrary VPA' path."}, {"id": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_test_suite", "label": "Test Suite T-1 to T-25", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}], "edges": [{"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "interview_transcript_yeshu", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "perflo_docs_agents__overview_perflo", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.85}, {"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "interview_transcript_yeshu_yeshu_agarwal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "interview_transcript_yeshu_hemant_kumar", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_ap_agent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0", "target": "prd_perflo_ap_agent_v0_ingest_worker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "PRD_PERFLO_AP_AGENT_V0.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 0.9